4, 3, 2, or 1 (but not 0 because \\( V > S \\)).\n   - If \\( V = 6 \\), then \\( S = 0 \\) (not valid because \\( V > S \\)).\n   - If \\( V = 5 \\), then \\( S = 1 \\).\n   - If \\( V = 4 \\), then \\( S = 2 \\).\n   - If \\( V = 3 \\), then \\( S = 3 \\) (not valid because \\( V > S \\)).\n   - If \\( V = 2 \\), then \\( S = 4 \\) (not valid because \\( V > S \\)).\n   - If \\( V = 1 \\), then \\( S = 5 \\) (not valid because \\( V > S \\)).\n\n5. If \\( C = 8 \\), then \\( V \\) can be 7, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2, or 1 (but not 0 because \\( V > S \\)).\n   - If \\( V = 7 \\), then \\( S = 0 \\) (not valid because \\( V > S \\)).\n   - If \\( V = 6 \\), then \\( S = 1 \\).\n   - If \\( V = 5 \\), then \\( S = 2 \\).\n   - If \\( V = 4 \\), then \\( S = 3 \\).\n   - If \\( V = 3 \\), then \\( S = 4 \\) (not valid because \\( V > S \\)).\n   - If \\( V = 2 \\), then \\( S = 5 \\) (not valid because \\( V > S \\)).\n   - If \\( V = 1 \\), then \\( S = 6 \\) (not valid because \\( V > S \\)).\n\n6. If \\( C = 9 \\), then \\( V \\) can be 8, 7, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2, or 1 (but not 0 because \\( V > S \\)).\n   - If \\( V = 8 \\), then \\( S = 0 \\) (not valid because \\( V > S \\)).\n   - If \\( V = 7 \\), then \\( S = 1 \\).\n   - If \\( V = 6 \\), then \\( S = 2 \\).\n   - If \\( V = 5 \\), then \\( S = 3 \\).\n   - If \\( V = 4 \\), then \\( S = 4 \\) (not valid because \\( V > S \\)).\n   - If \\( V = 3 \\), then \\( S = 5 \\) (not valid because \\( V > S \\)).\n   - If \\( V = 2 \\), then \\( S = 6 \\) (not valid because \\( V > S \\)).\n   - If \\( V = 1 \\), then \\( S = 7 \\) (not valid because \\( V > S \\)).\n\nNow we can count the valid assignments:\n- \\( C = 4 \\), \\( V = 3 \\), \\( S = 2 \\)\n- \\( C = 4 \\), \\( V = 2 \\), \\( S = 1 \\)\n- \\( C = 5 \\), \\( V = 4 \\), \\( S = 0 \\) (not valid)\n- \\( C = 5 \\), \\( V = 3 \\), \\( S = 1 \\)\n- \\( C = 6 \\), \\( V = 5 \\), \\( S = 0 \\) (not valid)\n- \\( C = 6 \\), \\( V = 4 \\), \\( S = 1 \\)\n- \\( C = 6 \\), \\( V =